course: dictionary
lesson: 4807
title: Humour: many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Humour is the quality of being funny, or the ability to see what is funny and laugh. Writers use it to entertain you: «The book is full of humour.» Here it means the jokes and silly moments that make the story funny.
explain: «She has a good sense of humour.» This means she can spot what is funny and enjoy a laugh. Other phrases tell you what kind of funny it is, such as «dry humour» or «toilet humour».
explain: Humour can also be a verb. «Just humour him» means go along with what he wants to keep him happy, even if you do not agree. Check the clues: he wants something, and you give in to keep the peace.
explain: Humour can be kind or hurtful. Kind humour makes everyone laugh together. Humour at someone's expense is unkind, because it laughs at them. Not every joke lands, and that is okay.
fact: Humour means jokes, funny situations, or the ability to laugh at them.
fact: «Humour» is a noun, and «to humour» someone is a verb meaning to go along with what they want.
fact: Before -ous, the u in -our usually drops: humour, humorous; glamour, glamorous.
fact: «Humour» can stop small teasing, but if it keeps going or is about your family, tell an adult.
fact: An older meaning of humour is a mood: «in a good humour» means in a good mood.
exercise: «The book is full of humour.» What does humour mean here? | *The quality of being funny | A long, boring chapter | A kind of weather | A type of book cover
exercise: «Just humour him.» What does humour mean here? | Ignore him completely | Argue with him until he gives up | *Go along with what he wants to keep him happy | Tell him a joke
exercise: Add -ous to humour, using the spelling rule. Which word is correct? | humorus | humourus | humourous | *humorous
test: «She has a good sense of humour.» What does this mean? | *She can spot what is funny and enjoy a laugh | She is always angry | She never laughs at anything | She cannot tell a joke from a story
test: Which example is unkind humour? | *Laughing at someone's mistake to hurt them | Telling a pun in class | Making everyone laugh together at a silly story | A joke about a silly animal
exam: «He was in a good humour all day.» What does in a good humour mean? | Very tired | *In a good mood | Lost | Hungry
